From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 05:57:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: replace wifi config with wifi-detect in ieee80211 hotplug

The ieee80211 hotplug ran 'wifi config' concurrently with the boot-time
uci-defaults scripts writing the wireless config. uci batch is not
atomic and its commit truncates the shared delta file, so concurrent
writers corrupt /etc/config/wireless: radio sections land mid-file and
uncommitted options are silently lost.

Config generation moved to the uci-defaults sequence, so drop the
'wifi config' call and run 'wifi-detect' in its place.
'wifi-detect' is what refreshes /etc/board.json's wlan hardware capabilities,
and those still need refreshing here: init.d/boot runs 'wifi config'
before the phys register, and board.json is regenerated every boot,
so otherwise the wlan caps stay empty and the ucode iwinfo reports
no modes on every boot after the first.
wifi-detect only rewrites /etc/board.json and touches no uci state,
so it does not reintroduce the config race.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
---
 src/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/10-wifi-detect |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/10-wifi-detect
+++ b/src/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/10-wifi-detect
@@ -1,6 +1,9 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
+# wireless config generation happens in the uci-defaults sequence;
+# running 'wifi config' here raced those scripts' uncommitted changes
 [ "${ACTION}" = "add" ] && [ -f /etc/board.json ] && {
-	/sbin/wifi config
+	# but board.json's wlan caps still need refreshing once the phys are up
+	ucode /usr/share/hostap/wifi-detect.uc
 	ubus call network.wireless retry
 }
